  "readme": "**Author :** 5argon,  https://arkham-starter.com\n\nThis box is designed with quite a lot of specific requirements, the most notable is the long slot for act / agenda block stand that ended up being a major constraint affecting everything!\n\n# What goes where\n\n- A + B : Core encounter cards, Brethren of Ash cards, player reference cards.\n- C + D : All basic weakness you have.\n- E1 + E2 : Damage / horror tokens (1+3). It's too thin for 3 fingers to jam inside but just thumb and index to pinch the tokens out works ok.\n- F1 (top) : Clue / doom (1+3)\n- F2 (bottom) : Resources (1, 3, 5)\n- E1 (top) : Free space for numbered dices, colored wood blocks, etc.\n- E2 (bottom) : Lead investigator token, connection arrows, 5 flashlight tokens.\n- H : Cram active chaos bag with tokens inside here.\n- I : Inactive chaos tokens. Two trays, each fitting 16+16 tokens with center divider.\n\n# Details\n\n- A fixed content box that goes with you no matter what you are playing, without ever requiring to change its content on switching campaigns. The campaign cards and player's deck needs to be elsewhere. Any future player cards purchased will only add a few Basic Weakness to this box.\n- There's a slot for act / agenda stand as long as it is not longer than the long edge of the box. I've allocated 3 cm for this compartment. Bottom of this compartment is padded up with 2 removable boxes, otherwise your hand cannot reach down to pick up the stand. Lids are included for those bottom inner boxes to prevent spilling.\n- I've measured sleeved core encounter sets, plus Brethren of Ash cards, plus 5 player reference cards, to require 8 cm. There's a 8 cm slot to fit exactly this. Center lowered divider to prevent cards from falling over while quantity is reduced when you are playing.\n- Whenever a campaign requires adding random basic weakness this box ensure you have all of them with you. I've went back to measure the entirety of Chapter 1's Basic Weakness (full collection, including Return To) to be also around 8 cm, so an another compartment future-proofed expecting Chapter 2 at around year 2032 (?) reach similar amount. You will only have 15 basic weakness if you bought just all the Chapter 2 Evergreen contents however (not even 1 cm), and might require some padding for them to not fall over until game gets bigger.\n- Removable chaos token containers calculated to fit 64 coins. Game comes with 44 coins, which if Chapter 2 decided to implement Bless and Curse, that'll add up to 64 coins so I want to future-proof it. In order to stack 2 tokens on top of each other in one box, I had to reduce the headroom to be less than the original box's headroom. The space is enough for each capsuled token if they are not more than 27 mm.\n- Narrow slot which your hand can't reach the bottom, used for storing active Chaos Bag with Chaos Tokens inside it, so you are not required to take the tokens out of the bag back to the dedicated coin slots.\n- 4 generic removable trays for tokens, in addition to 2 long ones that's under the stand.\n",
  "secondaryBase": true
